WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:24.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:27.374 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:28.379 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of that day.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.936 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:30.936 --> 00:00:32.698 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:35.715 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:39.222 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:41.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A range is the top and the bottom,

00:00:41.876 --> 00:00:44.256 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two lines,

00:00:44.256 --> 00:00:46.554 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:49.112 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:49.112 --> 00:00:51.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the range.

00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:53.424 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:53.424 --> 00:00:55.324 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:56.248 --> 00:00:57.756 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in

00:00:57.756 --> 00:00:59.696 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:00.896 --> 00:01:03.186 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:04.193 --> 00:01:06.038 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:07.770 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:08.878 --> 00:01:11.703 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook, the three

00:01:11.703 --> 00:01:14.186 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words from lesson one, range, levels

00:01:14.186 --> 00:01:16.412 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and stop, the pair, paper or a demo

00:01:16.412 --> 00:01:18.810 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
account, no secrets, a written stop,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.378 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the word Example on every figure.

00:01:21.898 --> 00:01:23.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:25.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:25.139 --> 00:01:26.257 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:26.509 --> 00:01:27.850 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.470 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawing a grid with no edges.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.125 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you

00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:32.577 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and what you pay with.

00:01:32.952 --> 00:01:34.416 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:34.416 --> 00:01:35.950 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.648 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:39.141 --> 00:01:40.873 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:42.954 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:43.364 --> 00:01:44.873 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair is

00:01:44.873 --> 00:01:46.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:47.031 --> 00:01:49.224 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:49.744 --> 00:01:51.163 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:01:51.163 --> 00:01:52.112 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of the day.

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:54.057 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:55.622 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.165 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:58.571 --> 00:02:01.156 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:01.676 --> 00:02:03.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.649 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:06.169 --> 00:02:08.535 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:08.535 --> 00:02:10.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

00:02:10.602 --> 00:02:12.781 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:13.215 --> 00:02:15.563 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

00:02:15.563 --> 00:02:18.058 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a daily close finishes outside the range

00:02:18.058 --> 00:02:20.553 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.893 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:22.893 --> 00:02:24.562 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:27.093 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the three

00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:28.993 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:29.863 --> 00:02:31.986 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:32.302 --> 00:02:34.201 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:34.201 --> 00:02:35.608 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:37.525 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:37.525 --> 00:02:38.992 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:39.512 --> 00:02:41.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:41.854 --> 00:02:44.196 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account,

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:46.383 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and sometimes move money out of it.

00:02:46.903 --> 00:02:49.529 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:49.529 --> 00:02:51.902 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:52.422 --> 00:02:54.221 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.696 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:57.171 --> 00:02:58.802 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:02:58.802 --> 00:03:00.588 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:01.638 --> 00:03:03.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the range onto the page,

00:03:03.612 --> 00:03:05.054 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not every day's prices.

00:03:05.574 --> 00:03:07.808 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:07.808 --> 00:03:09.956 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:11.929 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:03:11.929 --> 00:03:13.269 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the range.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.095 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:16.145 --> 00:03:17.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, range,

00:03:17.762 --> 00:03:19.216 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:19.736 --> 00:03:21.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with no

00:03:21.951 --> 00:03:24.018 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:26.321 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:03:26.321 --> 00:03:28.493 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the range

00:03:28.493 --> 00:03:30.587 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:30.587 --> 00:03:32.371 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:33.421 --> 00:03:35.432 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:35.928 --> 00:03:37.889 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:39.850 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:42.309 --> 00:03:43.832 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:43.832 --> 00:03:45.126 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:45.646 --> 00:03:47.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:47.558 --> 00:03:49.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:50.479 --> 00:03:52.546 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:52.896 --> 00:03:54.739 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:55.123 --> 00:03:56.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.010 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.653 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:01.778 --> 00:04:02.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:03.355 --> 00:04:04.751 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:05.252 --> 00:04:06.984 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:07.318 --> 00:04:10.509 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the July

00:04:10.509 --> 00:04:13.601 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window, the public

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:16.293 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

00:04:16.293 --> 00:04:18.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October 2023, so you buy the base,

00:04:18.886 --> 00:04:21.679 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

00:04:21.679 --> 00:04:24.371 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:24.891 --> 00:04:26.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:27.108 --> 00:04:29.284 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:29.284 --> 00:04:31.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:34.062 --> 00:04:35.968 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.484 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:42.119 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:47.357 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the July to October example window

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:51.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.360 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.809 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:04:57.809 --> 00:04:59.807 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:05:00.327 --> 00:05:02.183 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:05:02.183 --> 00:05:04.194 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:05:04.627 --> 00:05:06.517 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you

00:05:06.517 --> 00:05:08.486 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
got it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:08.486 --> 00:05:10.375 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:11.425 --> 00:05:12.696 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has

00:05:12.696 --> 00:05:14.037 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to say what you will do.

00:05:14.487 --> 00:05:16.294 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places

00:05:16.294 --> 00:05:18.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:19.224 --> 00:05:21.346 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the range,

00:05:21.346 --> 00:05:23.103 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom,

00:05:23.103 --> 00:05:25.225 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the second close still outside.

00:05:25.745 --> 00:05:27.309 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:27.309 --> 00:05:28.897 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders,

00:05:28.897 --> 00:05:30.797 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:31.308 --> 00:05:33.096 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:34.058 --> 00:05:36.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:36.788 --> 00:05:39.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.821 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:41.821 --> 00:05:43.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:44.141 --> 00:05:46.444 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:05:46.444 --> 00:05:48.376 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and

00:05:48.376 --> 00:05:50.604 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the exchange runs it, not this course.

00:05:51.124 --> 00:05:53.128 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:05:53.128 --> 00:05:54.983 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:05:55.503 --> 00:05:57.570 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.134 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:05:59.395 --> 00:06:01.937 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services

00:06:01.937 --> 00:06:04.556 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:04.556 --> 00:06:07.175 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:07.175 --> 00:06:09.487 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:10.007 --> 00:06:11.271 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:11.271 --> 00:06:12.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:13.123 --> 00:06:15.301 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:18.065 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:18.492 --> 00:06:20.726 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:23.601 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:24.121 --> 00:06:26.003 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:26.003 --> 00:06:27.233 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:30.224 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, new licensing rules

00:06:30.224 --> 00:06:32.859 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for platforms that hold crypto for you

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:35.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
are phased in through that year.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.531 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:37.659 --> 00:06:39.639 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:41.092 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:06:42.124 --> 00:06:43.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.238 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password, is two-factor authentication.

00:06:46.758 --> 00:06:48.858 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:06:49.378 --> 00:06:51.411 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:06:51.997 --> 00:06:53.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:55.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:59.010 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is an order that actually trades.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.821 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:04.153 --> 00:07:05.829 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:05.829 --> 00:07:07.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:07.898 --> 00:07:09.596 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:09.596 --> 00:07:11.295 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:11.815 --> 00:07:13.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:14.720 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:15.128 --> 00:07:17.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:21.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:21.551 --> 00:07:24.312 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:24.832 --> 00:07:26.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:27.276 --> 00:07:29.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.052 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:31.572 --> 00:07:33.610 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:35.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the July

00:07:35.192 --> 00:07:36.862 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window.

00:07:37.382 --> 00:07:39.693 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:39.693 --> 00:07:42.170 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.811 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:07:46.876 --> 00:07:48.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:07:51.419 --> 00:07:53.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin designed

00:07:53.519 --> 00:07:55.135 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay near the value of

00:07:55.135 --> 00:07:57.235 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a currency such as the US dollar.

00:07:57.755 --> 00:07:59.375 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:07:59.843 --> 00:08:02.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A swap is trading one coin for another.

00:08:02.477 --> 00:08:04.465 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price is in a stablecoin,

00:08:04.465 --> 00:08:05.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill is a swap.

00:08:06.787 --> 00:08:08.993 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated record

00:08:08.993 --> 00:08:10.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of every bot: the plan,

00:08:10.285 --> 00:08:12.186 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the changes, the fills, the fees,

00:08:12.186 --> 00:08:14.087 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a review note of what happened,

00:08:14.087 --> 00:08:16.293 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and whether you followed the rules.

00:08:16.813 --> 00:08:18.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:18.949 --> 00:08:21.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:21.604 --> 00:08:23.916 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

00:08:23.916 --> 00:08:25.866 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every swap goes in the journal.

00:08:26.386 --> 00:08:28.671 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is also the page you will

00:08:28.671 --> 00:08:30.880 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:08:33.926 --> 00:08:35.978 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

00:08:35.978 --> 00:08:38.424 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the value

00:08:38.424 --> 00:08:40.634 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars at the time,

00:08:40.634 --> 00:08:43.081 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

00:08:43.081 --> 00:08:45.369 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it was for, and who the other side was.

00:08:45.889 --> 00:08:47.963 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:08:47.963 --> 00:08:49.730 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, the gaps, the money

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:51.190 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in the bot, the stop rule,

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.341 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fills, the fees, the Australian

00:08:53.341 --> 00:08:55.492 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar value of each fill, a review

00:08:55.492 --> 00:08:57.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:08:58.009 --> 00:08:59.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The Australian dollar value

00:08:59.646 --> 00:09:01.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column is the one exception.

00:09:01.735 --> 00:09:03.243 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is for your tax records.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.864 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:09:05.864 --> 00:09:07.875 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:09:08.296 --> 00:09:09.301 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records

00:09:09.301 --> 00:09:10.642 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for at least five years.

00:09:10.998 --> 00:09:12.771 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:09:12.771 --> 00:09:13.657 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:09:14.177 --> 00:09:15.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:16.384 --> 00:09:17.547 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.357 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:20.492 --> 00:09:21.665 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:22.114 --> 00:09:23.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:24.618 --> 00:09:26.868 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:28.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for a seed phrase, a private

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.034 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret.

00:09:30.554 --> 00:09:32.530 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:33.953 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, or asks for one

00:09:33.953 --> 00:09:35.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of those, treat it as a scam.

00:09:36.132 --> 00:09:37.361 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:09:38.374 --> 00:09:40.825 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:09:40.825 --> 00:09:42.988 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:09:43.509 --> 00:09:44.515 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:09:45.505 --> 00:09:47.502 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now cover the chart and say your

00:09:47.502 --> 00:09:49.498 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
page out loud: the pair, the range,

00:09:49.498 --> 00:09:51.110 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the stop rule.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.631 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

00:09:53.631 --> 00:09:55.324 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:09:55.844 --> 00:09:57.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:09:57.964 --> 00:10:00.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:10:00.604 --> 00:10:02.434 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase,

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:04.631 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a private key, or an API secret.

00:10:05.151 --> 00:10:06.827 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:10:07.225 --> 00:10:08.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own

00:10:08.903 --> 00:10:10.791 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
notebook so a practice sketch is

00:10:10.791 --> 00:10:12.888 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
never later mistaken for a live plan.

00:10:13.938 --> 00:10:16.318 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:10:16.318 --> 00:10:18.459 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:18.459 --> 00:10:20.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.942 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What is a grid bot.

00:10:24.462 --> 00:10:26.082 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your range,

00:10:26.082 --> 00:10:27.702 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:10:27.944 --> 00:10:29.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:10:29.302 --> 00:10:30.592 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:10:31.112 --> 00:10:32.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

